# Web SPA Path Fallback

## Rule
Browser path routing requires SPA fallback support. During development and production, any unknown HTTP path (for example `/offers`, `/categories`, `/account`, `/admin/stores/new`, `/admin/products/new`, `/admin/categories/new`, `/m/wildbird`, `/products/…`) must serve the application entry (`index.html`) instead of returning 404. Navigation 3 can only restore routes after the application has been loaded. The routing layer is responsible only for mapping `window.location.pathname` to `Route`; the web server is responsible for delivering the application for every valid route.

## Development (this repo)
- Dev server: `:webApp:wasmJsBrowserDevelopmentRun` / `:webApp:jsBrowserDevelopmentRun` (webpack-dev-server).
- Kotlin 2.4.x `DevServer` DSL has no `historyApiFallback` property.
- Enable via [`webApp/webpack.config.d/spa-history-fallback.js`](webApp/webpack.config.d/spa-history-fallback.js) (auto-merged by KotlinWebpack `configDirectory`).
- That snippet also proxies Shopify CDN paths (`/shopify-assets-proxy`, `/cdn-shopify-proxy`) so Coil on Wasm/JS can load mock hero images without CORS (see `resolveNetworkImageUrl`).
- `resolveNetworkImageUrl` must return **absolute** `http(s)://origin/proxy/...` URLs — Coil ignores relative `/proxy/...` (no scheme → no fetch, silent placeholders).
- Proxy `headers` should include a browser `User-Agent` (Shopify assets CDN can 403 without one).
- Restart the browser run task after changing webpack snippets or `resolveNetworkImageUrl`.

## Production
Configure the host to rewrite app paths to `index.html` (nginx `try_files`, Cloudflare/Netlify/Vercel SPA rewrites). Do not hardcode domains in routing code.

## Do not
- Treat `Cannot GET /path` 404 as a Navigation 3 bug.
- Upgrade Kotlin/CMP solely to get a different webpack DSL for this.
